# Wet Brining

Wet brining involves soaking protein in a salt water bath for hours to days, resulting in juicy, seasoned meat throughout.

## How It Works

- Salt water bath (hours to days)
- Seasoning penetrates throughout the protein
- Result: juicy, well-seasoned meat

## Examples

- Whole turkey
- Pork shoulder

## Combination Technique

Wet brine first (12–24 hours), then dry rub before cooking, for the best of both worlds.

